# Golden cases are committed ONLY when synthetic. This rule used to be
# `evals/golden/*.json`, written when the golden set was expected to hold real
# client matters — and it then swallowed the synthetic cases authored
# specifically so they COULD ship. A fresh clone got no golden set at all: the
# free scorer skipped in full and three tests in test_api_practice.py failed
# outright, so the harness that guards every catalogue pattern was not running
# for anyone but its author.
#
# So the boundary is a directory, not a glob. A case built from a real matter
# goes in evals/golden/private/ and never leaves the machine;
# tests/test_golden_set.py loads only the top level and enforces
# `"synthetic": true` plus a provenance note on everything it finds there.
evals/golden/private/
evals/results/
